# Vellum USER symbol library -- the scratch file SymEdit edits by default.
# Draw your own parts with SymEdit (or by hand; the format is plain text,
# coordinates in QUARTER grid units, 4 = one grid unit):
#   symbol CODE PFX     start a symbol (PFX = designator prefix, - = none)
#   s x0 y0 x1 y1       line segment
#   c cx cy r           circle
#   t x y C             one small-font character
#   p x y               connection pin -- MUST sit on whole grid units
#                       (multiples of 4); wires snap onto pins
#   end                 finish the symbol (pins go BEFORE it)
# The origin (0 0) is the point Vellum places and rotates the symbol around.
# Once this file holds symbols, Vellum lists it in the palette as "symbols".
# The stock parts live in /usr/vellum/lib/discrete.sym and logic.sym.
